Customer-Support Agent for an Apparel Company — Candidate Task (1 hour)
 Build from scratch; do not reuse previous work. AI tools are allowed.
 Share your whole screen and think aloud throughout; the session is recorded.
 
Data: create fictional products (including some sale items), policies, customers and orders.

Agent: it answers customer questions and handles returns, refunds and cancellations. It clarifies, or escalates to a human, when information is missing or an action is unsafe.

Policies:
 (a) returns within 30 days of delivery;
 (b) sale items are exchange-only, except defective sale items, which can be refunded.
 For anything this brief does not specify, decide, and record each decision in ASSUMPTIONS.md.
Evals: repeatable, with explicit pass/fail criteria. You choose what to cover; we will judge your coverage against what can go wrong for a support agent that can issue refunds. Keep the output of every run, including failing runs, in eval_runs/.

We will test your agent after you submit, with messages you have not seen, against your own data. So:
it must run with one command documented in the README, taking a customer identity (customer ID or guest email) and a message, and printing the reply plus any action taken (refund, exchange, cancellation, escalation);
it must keep state between calls, so a repeated request is recognised;
there must be a documented way to make the order-lookup tool fail;
any model API key is read from an environment variable. No credentials in the ZIP.
Fix one failure: pick the worst failure in your eval_runs/, fix it, and add a test.
